# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHAT VERCEL IS ALLOWED TO PUBLISH , AN ALLOWLIST, 2026-10-03
#
# IT WAS A DENYLIST AND IT NAMED EIGHT API FILES. Everything else in the repo
# would have been served as a static asset the moment the production branch
# flipped: 87 .md files INCLUDING CLAUDE.md, 328 files under migrations/, 105
# _demo_*.html, 97 .csv data captures, 50 .sql, 44 under docs/. So
# vvonderxi.com/CLAUDE.md would have returned the whole playbook , every known
# defect, the database shape, the staging tables , alongside DATA_DEFECTS.md,
# SILENT_FAILURES.md and QA_PASS.md.
#
# NOTHING WAS EVER LIVE. The production branch `coming-soon` ships exactly nine
# files. This is a pre-FLIP blocker, not a breach that happened.
#
# AN ALLOWLIST RATHER THAN A LONGER DENYLIST, AND THE REASON IS THE FAILURE
# DIRECTION. A denylist has to be edited every time a new kind of file is added
# and fails OPEN when somebody forgets , which is exactly how 328 migration
# files came to be publishable. An allowlist fails CLOSED: a new file is not
# served until it is named here, and a missing asset is loud where a published
# secret is silent.
#
# THE LIST IS DERIVED, NOT GUESSED. Every `src`, `href` and `url()` in the ten
# shipping pages was extracted and resolved against disk, then the manifest's
# own icon list on top. That pass is what caught `vv-margin.js` and
# `manifest.webmanifest`, neither of which was in the original brief.
#
# IF YOU ADD AN ASSET, ADD IT HERE. The symptom of forgetting is a 404 for that
# one file on the deployed site and nothing locally, because the dev server
# serves everything.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Dotfiles first. Vercel does not normally serve a leading-dot path, but `/*` does
# not reliably exclude them through every matcher, and `.env.example` came through
# the first simulation of this file. Relying on the platform's default would be
# trusting a behaviour instead of stating one.
/.*

# Exclude everything at the top level, then name what comes back.
# `/*` is deliberate: a bare `*` would also exclude the CONTENTS of directories
# re-included below, and gitignore syntax cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded.
/*

# ── the ten shipping pages ────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/index.html
!/rankings.html
!/card.html
!/compare.html
!/playbook.html
!/vvindex.html
!/contact.html
!/iwonder.html
!/myclub.html
!/preferences.html

# ── shared modules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/vv-core.js
!/vv-marks.js
!/vv-margin.js

# ── icons, manifest and the social image ──────────────────────────────────
# icon-512 and icon-maskable-512 are referenced by the MANIFEST rather than by
# any page, and og-image.png only by a meta tag, so none of the three appears
# in a naive scan of src/href. Leaving them out breaks the installed-app icon
# and every unfurled link, both of which fail silently.
!/favicon.ico
!/favicon.svg
!/apple-touch-icon.png
!/icon-192.png
!/icon-512.png
!/icon-maskable-512.png
!/og-image.png
!/manifest.webmanifest

# ── directories ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/assets
!/api

# ── vercel's own config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept because the platform reads it from the deployment: it carries the
# headers block and `fluid`, and excluding it silently drops both.
!/vercel.json

# ── and the api files that were already excluded, still excluded ──────────
# `!/api` above re-includes the whole directory, so the original denylist has
# to be restated. These are importers and probes that must never be deployed ,
# one of them, search-player.js, is the corruption path CLAUDE.md records.
/api/apifootball-probe.js
/api/bsd-probe.js
/api/import-players.js
/api/import-positions.js
/api/import-positions-v2.js
/api/import-standings.js
/api/verify-positions.js
/api/verify-squad-positions.js
